BERT
----
The pause model (breaks.lsw) was trained in part to match the predictions of BERT
(bert-base-uncased, released by Google under the Apache License 2.0). No part of BERT is
distributed.

  Jacob Devlin, Ming-Wei Chang, Kenton Lee, and Kristina Toutanova. "BERT: Pre-training of Deep
  Bidirectional Transformers for Language Understanding." NAACL 2019. arXiv:1810.04805.
  https://huggingface.co/google-bert/bert-base-uncased


CMU Pronouncing Dictionary
--------------------------
The lexicon is the CMU Pronouncing Dictionary, packed, and the letter-to-sound model was trained
on it. The lexicon also holds entries written for Lip Service, which are not part of the CMU
dictionary and are under the AGPL with the rest.

